Acknowledged: Orin Falke, the Ordell County agent, reports to the county board in 1959, in numbered paragraphs. He sets out a sound outline and does not claim a year for Article VII:
- the creamery organized 1889 and built 1891;
- the station opened 4 May 1896;
- 3.61 against Larrow Green's 3.78, a flat 0.19 gap;
- the 1911 borrowed glass for nine weeks;
- the $3,800 award on 4 May, after the dismissal on 30 April;
- the glass condemned 12 June 1923;
- nine pipettes measured 9 March 1958.

He wrongly gives the post-1924 average as 3.85 and first concedes the wet hay as a partial cause. A note added in press then prints Bulletin 214's actual finding (no more than 0.05 in winter, nothing in summer), withdraws the hay concession, and corrects Ivy from great-niece to granddaughter.
